def edit(i,text,reason):edits[i]=text;reasons[i]=reason
abstract='Regulatory assignments depend on association inputs and signal models. We screened 5,460 of 6,923 primary biliary cholangitis locus-gene-cell comparisons and evaluated a protocol-frozen 642-comparison subset. Matching variant support and disease statistics changed 15 and 19 classifications, respectively. Eight shared-signal (H4) calls became distinct-signal (H3), and ten changed conversely. Shared and distinct pairs coexisted in 32 of 92 H4-supported comparisons, while a FCRL3 T-cell assignment reversed between covariate models. Across 486,000 simulations, multi-signal inference reduced false sharing from 12.41% to 8.56% and shared-signal recovery from 32.99% to 26.66%; only 33.08% were pair-evaluable. IL12RB2 sharing in natural killer cells received external disease-study and chromatin support, whereas liver data showed detectability without corrected disease enrichment. These results support signal-specific, model-qualified regulatory attribution without establishing mediation or universal methodological superiority.'
assert len(abstract.split())<=150,len(abstract.split())
edit(6,abstract,'Compile abstract from the new evidence hierarchy; define H4/H3, retain coexisting pairs, model reversal, recovery loss and tissue boundary.')
edit(9,orig[9]+' Functional follow-up depends on resolving that uncertainty: a strongly associated gene in the wrong cell context can direct experiments toward a regulatory assignment that the genetic data do not support.','Add a concrete biomedical reason to care without claiming clinical efficacy.')
edit(13,'We used PBC to test the reliability of immune-cell regulatory attribution through a linked sequence of questions. A PBC-wide screen defined a bounded high-information subset. Matched-input single-causal arms then distinguished changes caused by variant support and disease-statistic definitions from differences remaining between complete inferential procedures. Signal-pair identity and covariate sensitivity established what a comparison-level label could mean. Truth-known simulations tested the trade-off between false sharing, recovery and credible-set discovery. Finally, representative FCRL3 B-cell and IL12RB2-NK assignments were examined across molecular-QTL resources, a different disease study system, linked chromatin and donor-level liver expression. This design asked which assignments persisted, why others changed, and where statistical support stopped short of mechanism.','Question-led roadmap now mirrors the actual Results and figure order.')
edit(16,orig[16].replace('(Figure 1b)','(Figure 1d)')+' The four-arm input contract is shown in Figure 1b; the complete adjacent transition matrices are provided in Supplementary Figure S1.','Expose input contract before A0/A1/A2/M and retain separate 184/455/3 cohorts.')
edit(17,orig[17]+' The H4-supported fraction describes this selected workload and is not an estimated prevalence across all PBC regulatory comparisons.','Keep conditional selection and dependent counting units visible with the first outcome summary.')
edit(19,'Input matching explained part of the bidirectional reclassification','Answer-oriented heading with a bounded inference.')
edit(22,orig[22].replace('Figure 2c','Figure 2c').replace('Figure 2d','Figure 2d'),'Retain complete 642 transition matrix and distinct A2 starting denominators; figure now has one statistical job.')
edit(23,orig[23].replace('FCRL3-CD8_ET remained H4 in A0, A1 and A2 but was H3 under the primary PF10 multi-signal analysis. ','')+' Reclassification was therefore defined by the matched-input starting state; the concrete FCRL3 model contrast is developed below.','Move the detailed counterexample to its owning Results module; retain historical denominator reconciliation.')
edit(24,orig[24].replace('Figure 2e','Figure 3b'),'Move PF10/PF50 sensitivity next to signal-specific semantics and the model-dependent exemplar.')
edit(25,orig[25].replace('Figure 2f','Figure 3a'),'Retain coexistence before interpreting a specific cell assignment.')
edit(38,'Signal sharing remained pair specific and model dependent','New owner for old Figure2e/f and FCRL3 results; one dominant scientific question.')
edit(39,orig[39].replace('(Figure 5a)','').replace('(Figure 5b)','(Figure 3d)').replace(' respectively .',' respectively.'),'Retain B-cell support as the matched gene contrast to the T-cell model reversal; remove redundant OneK-only plot.')
edit(40,orig[40].replace('Current FinnGen public output','The frozen FinnGen public output')+' Stability within a model did not establish correctness; truth-known simulations provided a complementary test.','Bridge model robustness to simulation without inventing chronological motivation or external replication.')
edit(41,orig[41].replace('Figure 5c','Figure 3c'),'Place the unresolved PF10/PF50 counterexample directly after global pair and model summaries.')
edit(26,'Simulation separated shared-signal decisions from discovery adequacy','Answer-oriented simulation heading; no superiority claim.')
edit(27,orig[27].replace('Figure 3a,D','Figure 4a,d'),'Synchronize figure numbering and panel-case error in old reference.')
edit(28,orig[28].replace('Figure 3b','Figure 4b'),'Keep conditional and unconditional estimands distinct.')
edit(29,orig[29].replace('Figure 3c','Figure 4c'),'Retain incomplete S2 false-sharing reduction alongside stronger S5 gain.')
edit(30,orig[30]+' LD-dependent decision rates are shown in Supplementary Figure S2.','Retain scenario dependence as visible supplement rather than generalize the finite simulation grid.')
edit(31,'IL12RB2 gained bounded external disease-study and chromatin support','Make external validation ceiling part of the heading.')
edit(34,orig[34].replace('Figure 4a','Supplementary Figure S3'),'Move repeated-release stability to supporting evidence; prioritize genuinely different disease-study support in main figure.')
edit(35,orig[35].replace('Figure 4b','Figure 5a').replace('both members of the OneK QTL credible set occurred in the FinnGen R13 disease credible set.','both members of the OneK QTL credible set occurred in the FinnGen R13 disease credible set (Figure 5b).'),'Show exact source-CS identity alongside external disease association instead of release scatter as primary panel.')
edit(36,orig[36].replace('Figure 4c','Figure 5c').replace('Figure 4d','Figure 5d')+' The peak-gene link was reported with PBMC as its best cell context and did not independently establish an NK-specific link.','Synchronize non-directional evidence links; preserve the PBMC-versus-NK source boundary.')
edit(37,orig[37]+' The updated regional disease-caQTL result in the S11 evidence family supersedes the earlier position-only chromatin interpretation retained in S8.','Resolve the historical S8/current S11 source tension without changing historical data bytes.')
edit(45,orig[45].replace('(Figure 6c)','(Figure 6)'),'Remove redundant tissue schematic while retaining the boundary-changing null in text and legend.')
edit(47,'This study identified three linked conditions for interpreting immune-cell regulatory assignments at PBC loci: association inputs must be coordinated, the supported signal pair must be specified, and stability must be separated from discovery adequacy and mechanism. Input coordination explained some classification changes but left strict H4-to-H3 and H3-to-H4 transitions. Signal-pair coexistence and the FCRL3 covariate-model reversal showed why a favorable gene-level label was insufficient. The simulations then placed those real-data changes within a truth-known trade-off, rather than treating every lower H4 count as evidence of better inference.','Replace chronological metric recap with a contribution-first interpretation that connects all primary results.')
edit(50,orig[50]+' Because factor number changed both the QTL phenotype specification and its matched LD, this contrast did not isolate an LD-only effect.','Name the unresolved alternative explanation underlying the headline counterexample.')
edit(53,orig[53].replace('The missing direct eQTL-caQTL posterior prevents this triangle from becoming evidence of causal mediation.','The missing direct eQTL-caQTL posterior, correlated source observations and the absence of an intervention prevent this triangle from establishing causal mediation.'),'Keep public evidence integration distinct from independent causal validation.')
edit(57,'Several limitations define the statistical claim ceiling. Only the high-information subset received multi-signal analysis, and repeated gene-cell comparisons were nested within 47 selected risk regions. Neither 92/642 nor the bidirectional transition counts estimate rates across all PBC comparisons. Real-data transitions have no known causal truth and therefore represent reclassification, not measured error correction. Matched support and disease statistics remove two alternative explanations, but ABF and SuSiE-based procedures still differ in discovery, priors, parameterization and decision rules. The simulation used two empirical 128-variant LD templates, fixed sample sizes and a finite grid; it evaluated single-configuration components rather than directly calibrating the complete cross-L and low-prior gate.','Separate statistical limits from biological-validation limits; preserve every material caveat and add locus dependence explicitly.')
extra_limit='The validation layers have distinct ceilings. OneK1K and TenK10K reused the same discovery PBC GWAS. FinnGen R13 supplied a different disease study system with 795 cases, but public metadata could not establish participant non-overlap, and the external analysis was single-causal rather than a second source-LD multi-signal fit. The chromatin triangle lacked a direct eQTL-caQTL posterior, and OMIX001122 provided one processed matrix per condition without spatial coordinates. The liver analysis had five donors per group, non-lesion surgical controls and a bounded target panel. Neither genetic sharing nor tissue detectability establishes that perturbing IL12RB2 or FCRL3 alters a PBC-relevant phenotype.'
edit(59,'At PBC risk loci, coordinated inputs and signal resolution changed which regulatory assignments were supported, while covariate sensitivity and limited credible-set discovery constrained their interpretation. External IL12RB2 evidence increased confidence in a regulatory association; FCRL3 exposed both reproducible B-cell sharing and a model-dependent T-cell assignment. Liver data established detectability without corrected disease enrichment. Reporting these layers separately makes functional prioritization more interpretable while preserving the distinction between statistical sharing and mechanism.','Land on the biomedical consequence and evidence ceiling without repeating every count.')
edit(113,orig[113].replace('r7c2-q1-journal-audit-dual-track-2026-10-11','r7c3f-full-audit-rebuilt-submission-2026-10-12'),'Point baseline public evidence to the verified reconstructed tag; new editorial draft remains local.')
edit(120,orig[120].replace('r7c2-q1-journal-audit-dual-track-2026-10-11','r7c3f-full-audit-rebuilt-submission-2026-10-12'),'Keep the cited public tag real and immutable.')
edit(105,orig[105]+' The reported fasthurdle peak-gene coefficient was 0.140574, with PBMC designated as its best cell context; this link was not treated as separately verified NK-specific linkage.','Keep chromatin source cell labels distinct from NK disease-QTL colocalization records.')
