sup.add_heading('Source-version interpretation',level=2);sup.add_paragraph('The S8 tables preserve the earlier molecular-resource and position-based chromatin audit. The later fixed-scope S11 query returned disease-caQTL colocalization at the linked IL12RB2 peak and supersedes that earlier positional ceiling. Both versions remain archived; current chromatin interpretation uses the S11 regional edges and retains the unavailable direct eQTL-caQTL posterior. A top variant missing from one peak credible set is not equivalent to absence of regional disease-caQTL sharing.')
sup.add_paragraph('S5 contains 2,568 comparison-configuration fit rows (642 comparisons × four fine-mapping configurations). The separate corrected kriging audit contains 2,568 comparison-model-trait units (642 × two models × two traits). The targeted source-identity gate contains 14 comparison-model rows from seven comparisons. Equal counts describe different objects and must not be merged.')
suppleg={1:'Complete adjacent-arm transitions in the frozen 642 comparisons. Panels a-c show A0-to-A1 support restriction, A1-to-A2 disease-statistic replacement and A2-to-M complete-procedure contrast. Counts include all states, not only H4/H3 reversals. Panel d distinguishes targeted model identity, four-configuration SuSiE fit rows and two-model/two-trait kriging units. One reviewed kriging variant was outside the credible sets and did not trigger refitting.',2:'Decision rates depend on LD architecture. Panels a-f correspond to S1-S6 defined in Methods. Unconditional ABF and matched multi-signal H4 rates are weighted by replicate counts within each target causal-pair r-squared level, averaging the frozen MAF, L, prior and template grid. In S2/S5 the H4 decision is false sharing; in the other scenarios it is shared-signal recovery. These are finite-grid component rates, not prevalence estimates or calibration of the full composite gate.',3:'FinnGen release stability is not a new independent cohort. Panel a compares source credible-set probabilities for the 17 members shared by R12 and R13; the two R12-only members are outside this scatter. Panel b uses the full source-set sizes: 19 R12 versus 17 R13 disease credible-set members; all 17 R13 members occur in R12 (Jaccard 17/19). Sequential releases are correlated and are not two independent disease replications.'}
